INSERT INTO cases VALUES(24,'TX-26-00990','191st District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2026-05-19','OPEN','TAX DELINQUENCY','Hector Lopez Lopez','[{"name": "Hector Lopez Lopez", "address": "10130 Shayna Dr., Dallas, TX 75217", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "private process server", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Primary defendant - In Personam"}, {"name": "Dan Leung", "address": "10130 Shayna Dr., Dallas, TX 75217", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "private process server", "isInRemOnly": true, "notes": "In Rem Only defendant"}]','10130 Shayna Dr., Dallas, TX 75217',NULL,'00000170764000000','LGBS (Linebarger)','JONES, STEPHEN EARL',19788.810000000001565,NULL,'[]',2,0,0,'[{"suitNumber": "TX-13-30765", "court": "14TH DISTRICT COURT", "style": "DALLAS COUNTY, ET AL VS. CORNELIA WEBB", "county": "Dallas County, Texas"}]',0,0,0,'Both defendants unserved as of last docket entry','medium',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,0,'2027-01-27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 1094.9, "penaltyInterest": 729.11, "total": 1824.01}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 1127.13, "penaltyInterest": 765.29, "total": 1892.42}, {"entity": "Dallas College", "taxAmt": 554.85, "penaltyInterest": 372.66, "total": 927.51}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO – TX-26-00990\n**PROPERTY:** 10130 Shayna Dr., Dallas, TX 75217 | **DEFENDANT:** Hector Lopez Lopez | **PRIORITY:** High\n\n---\n\n## PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is unquestionably a **land play with demolition costs factored**. The 940 SF structure built in 1935 (91 years old) shows 60% depreciation and has reached end-of-economic-life status. At $119,860 market value, the improvement-to-land ratio strongly suggests DCAD values the dirt more than the building. The dual-defendant situation reveals ownership complexity: Dan Leung appears as In Rem Only, suggesting either a quiet title cloud, failed ownership transfer, or mortgage interest. Prior case TX-13-30765 against Cornelia Webb (2013) shows this property has been through the foreclosure mill before—Webb''s payment history runs 2006, then Dallas County District Clerk made payments 2009-2012, indicating a prior tax foreclosure that may have had defective title work. Hector Lopez Lopez took deed 4/1/2016, made ONE payment in 2021, then went dark for four years. Zero homestead exemption confirms he''s never lived here—this is a failed flip, landlord burnout, or inherited problem. Payment history gap between 2016-2021 before his single payment screams financial distress. The structure''s age means foundation issues, outdated electrical/plumbing, likely code violations if rented. This isn''t fixable—it''s a scrape-and-build lot in Pleasant Grove.\n\n## FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nFiled at $19,788.81 (May 2026), live balance now sits at **$20,318.94**—a modest $530.13 acceleration over 8 months, indicating penalties/interest running roughly 3.2% of principal annually. Tax breakdown shows Dallas County ($1,824.01), Parkland Hospital ($1,892.42), and Dallas College ($927.51) as primary creditors. At $119,860 DCAD market value, the debt-to-value ratio is **17%**—extremely manageable and creates massive equity cushion for negotiation. Today''s payoff costs **$20,318.94 to the tax office**, but that number climbs $165/month as penalties compound. With no homestead exemption, no redemption rights complicate post-judgment acquisition. The prior 2013 suit against Webb suggests there may be a $15K-$25K title defect or prior lien still clouding this—Dan Leung''s In Rem','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01T23:55:33.886153','2026-07-07T12:38:34.034924','2026-07-07T12:38:34.034924',1,'individual','high','','{"account_number": "00000170764000000", "market_value": 119860, "land_value": 56550, "improvement_value": 63310, "estimated_annual_taxes": 2668.93, "year_built": 1935, "effective_year_built": 1935, "actual_age": 91, "building_class": "04", "construction_type": "FR