asset requiring capital investment. The payment history reveals **critical ownership chaos**: JONATHAN CASTILLO paid 2024-2025 taxes (those years now show $0 live balance), yet the lawsuit targets JUAN CARLOS ESTRADA MACIAS and IRMA ISELA MEDINA LOZOYA as current owners. Macias last paid in 2014, PATRICIA PORTER WILER (now served in rem only at a different address) paid in 2012, and LAUDERBACK paid in 2009. This fractured chain suggests unreleased deed transfers, quitclaim complications, or informal family transfers. **The fact that someone (Castillo) paid 2024-2025 taxes but isn''t named as defendant indicates either Linebarger''s research missed a transfer or there''s an unrecorded interest**—this is a title defect waiting to explode. The homestead exemption remains active, confirming someone is occupying the property, likely Castillo or a family member.\n\n## 2. FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nThe lawsuit filed for **$11,679.20** covering 2024-2025 delinquencies ($4,926.96 GISD + $3,044.14 City of Garland base taxes, plus $3,356.10 combined penalties/interest as of May 2025). However, DCAD live data now shows **$0.00 balance**—meaning taxes were paid after the suit was filed, likely by Castillo in mid-to-late 2026. At 8 months post-filing, penalties would have accrued another $420-480 before payoff, so actual satisfaction was approximately $12,100. **Debt-to-value ratio is now 0%**—there is no','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01T23:56:27.338518','2026-07-07T12:39:33.882529','2026-07-07T12:39:33.882529',1,'individual','high','LOT 43 LESS WEST 3 FEET, BLOCK 4, RIDGEWOOD ESTATES NO. 1 ADDITION, AS RECORDED IN INSTRUMENT 201300118341, OF THE DALLAS COUNTY DEED RECORDS','{"account_number": "26485500040430000", "market_value": 250840, "land_value": 65000, "improvement_value": 185840, "estimated_annual_taxes": null, "year_built": 1957, "effective_year_built": 1957, "actual_age": 69, "building_class": "12", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation":